  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-LA Sida FFA II - Laos Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fair Finance Asia Program (FFA) envisages to reduce the negative impact of national and cross-border bank investments in Asia on human rights, the environment and climate change, and to increase adequate financial services for pro-poor, inclusive economic development. The goal is to establish a sustainable financial sector in Asia, with financial sector institutions operating at national and regional level being more transparent and accountable and adhering to Economic, Social and Governance (ESG)-criteria. FFA is funded by Sida.

Oxfam in Laos will oversee the Fair Finance Laos from 2023 to 2027. Based on the project management approach, this project would be managed by National Resource and livelihood Program Manager and oversight by National Director and Cluster Director both Business Operational and program thematic parts. For the Business Operation or finance management, they would have CLV Finance and Grant Manager under the oversight of the Head of Business and Operation.

The project activities implementation and its progress would be reported as a timeline given by FFA as well as the financial report would be shared as agreed on the agreement we have.

Theresults of the project intervention as well as challenges and lesson learned would be brought to discuss in the annual program reflection workshop that would be organized once a year. This meeting would be involved program leaders and coordinators as well as the business operation team. In the meanwhile, the project holder would bring the lesson learned to share at the regional meeting levelswith another country that engage on the FFA approach.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam has had a presence in Lao PDR for longer than most INGOs, with both Oxfam in Belgium (OBE) and Oxfam Australia (OAU) beginning programming and establishing offices in the late 1980s.  Oxfam&#x2019;s vision is of a Laos in which all citizens &#x2013; particularlywomen, the marginalised and discriminated groups &#x2013; are able to claim their right to access opportunities and resources so as to overcome all forms of poverty and injustice.

Since 2015, the work of Oxfam in the country is governed by the Oxfam Country Strategy (2015-2019).We seek transformative changes in policies, practices and beliefs in ways that fundamentally improve the lives of poor and marginalised women and men, and ensure that all citizens have the same opportunities to enjoy their rights. Todo so, Oxfam focuses its work on four Domains of Change: Citizen Participation and Civil Society Development, Gender Justice, Resilient Communities and Sustainable Development, and Responsible Investment.

For this project, Oxfam in Laos will support theexpansion of the influencing work and public campaign on advocating for more inclusive social protection and access to social protection of the most marginalized workers. National public events will be organised, such Eliminate Violence Against Women Day(EVAW), and digital platforms will be used to socialize the information, and stir discussion and dialogue among rights holders, government stakeholders and policy makers. The campaigns will be implemented nationwide and in the provinces where Oxfam in Laos works. Target groups include marginalized workers, youth,women, CSOs as well as government stakeholders.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
